{"title":"2026 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 4a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a <i>Dunbar sequence</i>,\n</p>\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li>each term is a positive integer,</li>\n<li>the second term is greater than the first term, and</li>\n<li>each term after the second is calculated by adding the two previous terms in the sequence.\n</li></ul>\n<p>For example, the first six terms of the Dunbar sequence with first term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and second term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3c8bef9ece75fbff2fe0e15ee7b9737dde293cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 5, 7, 12, 19, 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"17\" /></center> \n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the fifth term in a Dunbar sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/1/4b14ef560acadba8244952e9a8d5481f494445dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$57$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and the third term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, what is the first term in the sequence?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/2/bd28b278a07bda0ea4d08737743613980c6aa6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> be the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /><sup>th</sup> term of the Dunbar sequence. Repeatedly using the fact that \"each term after the second is calculated by adding the two previous terms in the sequence\" for a Dunbar sequence, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a7083b682cd1c500acb46556df2f08ad861c097.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{3} + a_{4} = a_{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56c591273f8e2de7a37940eea7e6742530d32ba1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 + a_{4} = 57$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/9/7b90672e11f522f71d4e3fdab276e67603fc3a75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{4} = 57 - 20 = 37$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5aef86fc2046d4515f1f7eb02543ee599699cde6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2} + a_{3} = a_{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/a/b0a8709d0d929b17bac54cb13efa474bd31f4719.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2} + 20 = 37$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/e/88eb88c28e54dbf4003c009da5bc4911d85c2680.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2} = 37 - 20 = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/91954d18f1a364ac57ced0c1dbf237049ceb67ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1} + a_{2} = a_{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be8b224c085c306e81d647d4706b6a45bb429420.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1} + 17 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb723c08eba78b124ee27f03d32cbbd132fabd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1} = 20 - 17 = \\boxed{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"146\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018034646\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.017 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 63/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 556/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2933/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.877      1 2026_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4\n100.00%    6.877      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36901:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018034646 and revision id 285659. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}